.TH GALLANT 1
.SH NAME
gallant \- check files against rules with a decision model
.SH USAGE
.nf
gallant - check files against rules with a decision model

Usage:
  gallant [options] path...
  gallant [options] --diff
  gallant [options] --assume-filename name

Description:
  gallant checks files against rules. A rule gives one question to a decision
  model, and gallant prints one line for each answer. Rules are markdown files
  in .agents/gallant.

Input:
  With no --diff or --assume-filename, gallant checks the files and directories
  you name. An explicit file is always checked. A directory is walked, and each
  file whose name matches a rule is checked; hidden files and directories (names
  beginning with a dot) are skipped during the walk.

  --diff reads a unified diff from standard input and checks each changed file.
  --assume-filename reads one file from standard input and names it, so a pipe
  can stand in for a file. The two options are mutually exclusive and take no
  path operands.

Options:
  --provider name         model provider (default "opencode")
  --model name            model name (default from the provider)
  --rules dir             directory of lint rules (default ".agents/gallant")
  --jobs n                files to check concurrently (default 8)
  --include-passing       also print the rules the file passes
  --json                  print the answers as a JSON array
  --diff                  check a unified diff read from standard input
  --assume-filename name  check one file read from standard input under this name
  -h, --help              print this help and exit

Output:
  gallant prints one finding per line in a fixed, space-separated format:

    <file> <rule> <type> <confidence> <result>

  The format is line-oriented: every newline is escaped, so one finding stays on
  one line. For machine consumption, --json prints an array of objects instead:

    gallant --json

  A file that cannot be checked (for example, one too large for the model) is
  reported on standard error as "gallant: <file>: <reason>". The other files are
  still checked, and the run exits nonzero.

  A failure of the provider itself (an unreachable or erroring server) is
  reported once, not per file.

  If the rules directory holds no rules, a warning is printed and nothing is
  checked.

Exit status:
  0    all checks ran
  1    an error stopped the run
  2    no input, or conflicting options
  130  the run was interrupted

Examples:
  gallant .
  gallant main.go pkg/handler.go
  git diff HEAD~1 | gallant --diff
  printf 'package main\\n' | gallant --assume-filename main.go
  gallant --provider ollama --model nimble --jobs 16 .

Help topics:
  gallant --help rules      the rule format
  gallant --help providers  the provider list
.fi
.SH RULES
.nf
Rule format

  A rule is a markdown file. Put rules in .agents/gallant, or in the directory
  given with --rules. gallant reads rules in subdirectories and ignores hidden
  files.

  A rule has optional frontmatter between two "---" lines, then the rule text:

    ---
    appliesTo: "*.go"
    type: noul
    ---
    # No debugging leftovers

    Report a violation when the file keeps code that only helped while it was
    written.

Frontmatter fields:

  appliesTo      A glob, or a list of globs, matched against the file name (not
                 the path). gallant uses the rule only when a glob matches.

  type           The question the model answers. One of:

                   noul    asks whether the file breaks the rule, and reports a
                           violation above minConfidence.
                   choice  asks which option describes the file.
                   score   asks which level describes the file.

  criteria       For choice, a mapping of option to description. For score, an
                 ordered list of levels, from low to high.

  minConfidence  For noul only. The probability of a violation above which the
                 rule fails, from 0 to 1 (default 0.5).

  The rule text after the frontmatter is sent to the model as written; nothing
  is prepended or appended to it.

Examples:

  noul:

    ---
    appliesTo: "*.go"
    type: noul
    minConfidence: 0.8
    ---
    # Exported declarations need doc comments

    Report a violation when an exported declaration has no doc comment.

  choice:

    ---
    appliesTo: "*.go"
    type: choice
    criteria:
      useful: "The comments explain intent or rationale."
      mixed: "Some comments add value, others repeat the code."
      useless: "The comments mostly restate the code."
    ---
    Classify the comments in this file.

  score:

    ---
    appliesTo: "*.md"
    type: score
    criteria:
      - "Easy to read"
      - "Somewhat hard"
      - "Very hard"
    ---
    Rate how hard this document is to read.
.fi
.SH PROVIDERS
.nf
Providers

  Choose a provider with --provider and a model with --model. The default
  provider is opencode, and its default model is used when --model is omitted.

  opencode

    OpenCode Zen's System One gateway, serving TypeSafe's Jev.

    Models   jev-1.13, jev-1.13-free (default)
    API key  OPENCODE_API_KEY (required for jev-1.13; jev-1.13-free needs none)

      export OPENCODE_API_KEY=...
      gallant --provider opencode --model jev-1.13-free .

  cloudflare

    Cloudflare Workers AI, serving Cloudflare's Clef decision models. Clef reads
    up to 64K tokens and up to 64 rules per file.

    Models   clef (default), clef-flash
    API key  CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN (required; a Workers AI token)
    Account  CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID (required)

      export CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=... CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=...
      gallant --provider cloudflare --model clef-flash .

  ollama

    A local Ollama server (0.35.0+). No API key. Models are discovered from the
    server, for example nimble (default), tev1, clef, clef-flash, and laya.

    Base URL  OLLAMA_HOST (default http://127.0.0.1:11434)

      gallant --provider ollama --model nimble .

  strands-decider

    A local Strands Decider server (0.1.0+). No API key. The served checkpoint
    is discovered from the server, and defaults to
    strands-decider-2B-qwen3.5-v1-2610.

    The server truncates state larger than the checkpoint's context window (4,096
    tokens for the shipped checkpoints). Start it with --strict-window to reject
    an oversized file instead, which gallant reports as a file error.

    The server answers one request at a time, so gallant serialises evaluations
    for this provider and --jobs has no effect on throughput. Files are still
    reported in order.

    Base URL  STRANDS_DECIDER_HOST (default http://127.0.0.1:8000)

      pip install strands-decider
      strands-decider serve StrandsAgents/strands-decider-2B-qwen3.5-v1-2610 --port 8000
      gallant --provider strands-decider .
.fi
